---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/main.astro";
import Header from "@/components/header.astro";
import { HEv3QuicTlsTest } from "@/components/tests/hev3-quic-tls-test";
import Link from "@/components/link.astro";
---

<PageLayout title="HEv3 QUIC vs. TLS/TCP Test | Happy Eyeballs Webtester">
  <Header titleLine1="Happy Eyeballs" titleLine2="QUIC vs. TLS/TCP Test">
    <p>
      We operate a specialized web server capable of introducing artificial
      delays during the initial connection handshake based on the TLS SNI. The
      server listens for both TCP and UDP connections and responds with the
      negotiated HTTP protocol version (HTTP/3 or HTTP/2).
    </p>
    <p>
      Our DNS nameserver responds with HTTPS resource records for all test
      domains to signal HTTP/3 (QUIC) availability. For this test to function,
      your browser must query and respect these records. You can verify this
      using our
      <Link href="/tests/http3-availability">HTTP/3 availability tester</Link>.
    </p>
    <p>
      We simulate a range of handshake delays for both QUIC and TLS/TCP. Your
      browser will attempt connections for each delay, allowing us to observe if
      it handles the Happy Eyeballs version 3 race between both application
      layer protocols.
    </p>
    <p>
      We randomize domains to try to prevent caching effects on the browser's
      side as much as possible. Furthermore, we aggressively close connections
      on the server side after every request, forcing the browser to perform a
      new handshake for each test.
    </p>
  </Header>

  <HEv3QuicTlsTest client:load />
</PageLayout>
